        }
      ],
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected:** with `RUST_LOG=rayx_signalr::stateful=debug` the trace shows every received Ack and Sequence, including rejected ones (zero-id and undecodable), and the outcome of every resume, as `docs/11-errors-and-logging.md` and the skill's `troubleshooting.md` promise.\n\n**Observed (original):** rejected control messages and failed resends left no stateful record. After the first repair, zero-id and undecodable Ack/Sequence frames were still rejected inside the protocol decoders before reaching the buffer, so `reason=zero` was unreachable from real traffic.\n\n**Verified resolved:**\n- `decode_json_control` and `decode_messagepack_control` now return the raw id with the same logical type, arity and integer checks for both protocols.\n- `StatefulMessageBuffer::receive_control` records `ack-rejected` / `sequence-rejected reason=malformed` for a decode error. A decoded id goes to `acknowledge` / `reset_incoming_sequence`, which record `reason=zero|beyond-highest-sent|transport-active|gap` before returning the unchanged errors. Zero ids are still refused, as the hub-protocol rules require.\n- All four receiver sites (`run_receiver` JSON and MessagePack, WASM `process_frame` JSON and MessagePack) decode outside the lock or borrow, then call `receive_control`, and keep their previous error handling.\n- `should_process` records `receive-rejected reason=before-sequence`, and `finish_resend(completed)` records `resend-finished` or `resend-failed` on both resume paths.\n- `sequence_trace_records_rejected_control_messages_from_the_wire` and `sequence_trace_accepts_valid_control_messages_from_the_wire` drive the same decode-plus-`receive_control` path with JSON and MessagePack wire payloads (zero id, missing id, non-JSON, wrong type, wrong arity) and assert the exact records. The `s1-sequence-trace` check ran all 8 tests.",
      "boundaryId": "S1"
    },
    {
